ould prove by writing current health above max? Hmm.\n\nLet me just explore.\n\nFor rupee count: we can collect rupees on the overworld by killing enemies or cutting bushes. Actually the first screen has no enemies. We can scroll to screens with rupees. In Zelda 1 overworld there are often rupees under bushes/rocks, or in caves. Rupees can be found. Alternatively, use the \"money making game\" ... too complex. Simplest: walk around and kill enemies to drop rupees. Or find a screen with a rupee.\n\nActually, an easier trick: the bomb count and key count are also zero. To change them, we could buy from shop but need money. Hmm.\n\nBut differential search doesn't require changing the value by gameplay necessarily; but skill says make the value change by playing. For zero values we could use the fact that known HUD text changes. Alternatively we can use write_memory to change a candidate and see HUD... but that's circular (we need candidate first).\n\nAlternative approach: snapshot full RAM with values known: the HUD displays rupee X0 = \"00\"? Actually the count is 2 digits? Task says \"a rupee count (X0)\" meaning e.g. 0. The HUD shows digits.\n\nWe could find the digit tile indices in the nametable to read values. Hmm.\n\nBetter: We can do a differential where we change something and observe. For rupees, perhaps we can earn a rupee by defeating an enemy that drops one. Let me just play: from start screen, maybe there are screens with enemies nearby. Kill them and get rupees. First screen of Zelda is a tree/rock screen? Actually start screen (the one Link appears on) has a cave and an old man? No, Link starts on the screen with the cave to the left? Let me recall. New game start: Link on a screen with a cave entrance at top? The starting screen has a rock and... Actually the classic start: Link appears in a screen with a cave (the \"It's dangerous to go alone\" cave is one screen north). The start screen is grassy with a few trees.\n\nEnemies: Octoroks appear as you walk. Killing them may drop rupees (or hearts). Grinding for rupees works.\n\nPlan: use play_input to roam and kill enemies, checking rupee count by screenshot, until rupee > 0. Then snapshot/diff.\n\nBut diff requires capturing \"before\" and \"after\" around the change. We can snapshot before killing, then after collecting rupee. But random drops. Alternatively snapshot when rupee=0, then kill until rupee increases, then diff. That's fine.\n\nKeys: keys only appear in dungeons. To get a key you'd have to enter a dungeon and find a key. That's doable but long. Alternatively, in Zelda 1 overworld there is a screen with a key? Hmm. There's the \"rupee cave\"? No.\n\nHmm. Maybe there's a simpler approach: the values for bombs/keys/rupees are likely contiguous in RAM. If we find one (rupees) by differential search, bombs and keys are probably nearby (like rupee at $067D, keys $067E, bombs $067F). Then we prove each by write_memory and screenshot. The task explicitly says \"Use the find-variable skill and your own judgement for values that do not change by playing.\" So it acknowledges some values won't change by playing (bombs, keys at start = 0). So we can use judgement: find rupee by playing, then infer neighbors, prove by write.\n\nHearts: find current health by damage, and heart containers maybe adjacent or we can prove by writing.\n\nLet me start by loading the skill and getting a screenshot.\n\nLet me do skill call and screenshot in parallel."}
