mes while the game runs (resuming if paused?). Let me just try.\n\nPlan:\n- Ensure the game is running (unpause).\n- Position to die quickly (stand among enemies).\n- Call trace_writes(address=0x206C, mem_type=ppu, mode=write, frames=600) — but during those 600 frames I need the respawn HUD write. If the game is running and I'm among enemies, Link will die and show the menu, but CONTINUE requires input. trace_writes runs frames without input. So the HUD write may not happen.\n\nHmm. I need to time the CONTINUE press during the trace window. But trace_writes is a blocking tool call.\n\nAlternative: the HUD is written on room/cave load too! When entering a cave or dungeon, the whole screen (including HUD) is drawn. Does entering the sword cave redraw the HUD? Earlier, when we entered the cave, the HUD was visible and unchanged. If the HUD is redrawn on cave entry, then trace will catch it.\n\nAlso, on each overworld screen scroll, does the game redraw the HUD? In Zelda, the overworld scroll draws the new columns but NOT the HUD (HUD is static). Hmm.\n\nBut entering a cave/dungeon does a full screen load → HUD redraw. Let me test by tracing during a cave entry: start the trace, then walk into the cave. But trace_writes blocks...\n\nHmm, unless trace_writes runs the frames itself and I can't provide input. Let me check: maybe I should start the trace, and simultaneously... no, single-threaded.\n\nWait, maybe play_input and trace_writes can't overlap. But trace_writes says \"resume, play, or reset first\" — implying I trigger the event first, then trace? That doesn't make sense for a one-time event.\n\nLet me re-read: \"installs a callback on the range for N frames (default 60, max 600) and returns each writing PC... Refused while paused (frames must run); the game must actually perform the write during the window, so trigger the event (resume, play, or reset) first.\"\n\nHmm, \"trigger the event (resume, play, or reset) first\" — maybe it means the trace itself will run